## Context

0151 exit criterion: "Falsifiable hardening tests in CI (path-traversal,
input-DoS, update-integrity), each with a negative control." The existing
test suites cover contract invariants (0146) and data safety (0149) but not
adversarial input. This ticket adds a `security` test suite exercising the
attack surfaces enumerated in the 0151 threat model.

Update-integrity tests already exist in `test_update.sh` (hijack refusal,
offline, override). This ticket extends with path-traversal and input-DoS;
it does not duplicate the update tests.

## Relevant files
- `src/go/main.go` — `resolveDir`, `resolveTicketByID` (path construction)
- `src/go/new.go` — `cmdNew`, `slugify` (filename from title)
- `src/go/rm.go` — `cmdRm` (ID resolution + deletion)
- `src/go/archive.go` — `cmdArchive` (path construction)
- `src/go/atomicwrite.go` — `withinStore` (confinement, explicitly NOT security boundary)
- `src/go/erg.go` — `parseErgBytes` (parser, untrusted input)
- `src/go/ref.go` — `parseRef` (Blocked-by values)
- `src/go/validate.go` — validator rules

## Actions
1. Create `tests/test_security.sh` with these test groups:

   **Path traversal (ID/ref injection):**
   - `erg close ../../etc/passwd REASON` → must refuse (not escape store)
   - `erg log ../../etc/passwd LINE` → must refuse
   - `erg rm ../../etc/passwd` → must refuse
   - `erg new "normal title" ../../tmp` → must refuse or confine
   - Crafted .erg file with `Blocked-by: ../../../../etc/passwd` → must reject
   - Negative control: legitimate `erg close 9001 REASON` on a fixture → succeeds

   **Symlink escape:**
   - Create symlink `tickets/9002-symlink.erg` → `/tmp/target`; mutating
     commands must not follow the symlink out of the store
   - Negative control: real file at same path → succeeds

   **Input DoS:**
   - 10 MB .erg file → parser must not OOM or hang (bounded time)
   - 100,000-line log section → bounded parse time
   - Title with 10,000 characters → no ReDoS in slugify or titleStatusEdgeWord
   - Negative control: normal-sized .erg file → parses quickly

   **ID injection:**
   - Filename with embedded path separator: `0042/../../../etc.erg` → reject
   - Negative control: normal `0042-title.erg` → accepts

2. Add `security` to `TEST_SUITES` in Makefile.
3. Each test has an explicit negative control proving the check trips.

## Confinement fix (audit finding — raid 151 feasibility probe)

The audit probe found two real confinement gaps the write path (0149's
`writeTicketAtomic`/`withinStore`) does NOT cover. Fix both as part of this
ticket so the confinement tests are green:

- **`cmdRm` FILE form** (`rm.go`): the `.erg`-suffix branch calls
  `os.Remove(ticketPath)` directly, never `withinStore`. `erg rm
  /tmp/outside.erg` deletes a file outside the store. Add a `withinStore`
  gate against the resolved store before `os.Remove`. (HIGH: write path is
  confined, delete path was not — inconsistent rail.)
- **`cmdNew` DIR arg** (`new.go`): an explicit DIR is `filepath.Clean`ed then
  `MkdirAll`+created with no confinement. Confinement here is subtler — the
  store is the DIR itself, so the rail is "refuse a DIR that escapes the
  discovered/cwd store root" or document the explicit-DIR form as an
  intentional escape hatch. Match 0149's fail-safe philosophy; do not break
  the legitimate `erg new TITLE some/subdir` use.

Both attacks require attacker-controlled CLI args (not a committed `.erg`),
so the parser-input surface is unaffected. The fix closes the write/delete
consistency gap 0151's body flagged (`new`/`rm` path-injection in scope).

## Test
```sh
# Red: security suite should exist
make test-security
```

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `test_security.sh` covers path-traversal, symlink, input-DoS, ID injection
- [ ] Each positive test has a negative control (falsifiable)
- [ ] `cmdRm` FILE form refuses a target outside the resolved store
- [ ] `cmdNew` confines (or documents) the explicit-DIR form per 0149 philosophy
- [ ] All security tests pass (binary fixed in this PR)
- [ ] `make test` passes (all suites including security)
